# manifest.txt is signed byte-for-byte by NutriculaSignTool (LF line endings,
# signature covers the exact bytes). The GitHub Actions build runs on a
# Windows runner, whose git checkout converts text files to CRLF by default -
# that silently breaks the signature and makes the Broker reject the manifest
# (no network call, no -2). Git must never touch this file's line endings.
Assets/manifest.txt -text

# Everything else in Assets/ is a binary artifact whose SHA-256 is pinned in
# the manifest - never let git convert any of it either.
Assets/*.dll binary
Assets/*.exe binary
Assets/*.ex4 binary
Assets/*.ex5 binary
